{"type":"system","subtype":"background_tasks_changed","tasks":[{"task_id":"b210y3p3b","task_type":"local_bash","description":"cd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop; C=iter_3/candidate_4\ncat > $C/hypothesis.md << 'EOF'\nRefinement of the incumbent `personal_complement_symmetry_aversion`: each person still judges how random each sequence looks exactly as the incumbent does (personal ideal switching rate and sensitivity with lenience toward over-alternation, personal weights on imbalance, the longest streak and complement symmetry, shared weights on the final streak, mirror symmetry, run-length variety and the most lopsided stretch). The one change is in how a person acts on that impression: instead of a personal guessing rate that can only pull their choices toward a coin flip, each person has a signed engagement drawn from a population — most people follow their impression (more or less consistently), but a few have reversed the task and systematically choose the sequence that looks *less* random — so the model predicts that some people agree with the majority choice well below one half (the data contain people at 12–33% agreement), widening the spread of majority agreement across people that the critique (surviving FDR) says the incumbent under-produces.\nEOF\necho signed_engagement_complement_symmetry > $C/model_name.txt\npython3 - << 'EOF'\nsrc=open('models/personal_complement_symmetry_aversion.py').read()\nsrc=src.replace('''\"\"\"Personal complement-symmetry (antisymmetry) aversion.\n\nRefinement of complement_symmetry_aversion.''','''\"\"\"Signed personal engagement on top of personal complement-symmetry aversion.\n\nRefinement of personal_complement_symmetry_aversion. The one change: each\nperson's guessing rate becomes a signed engagement e in (-1, 1), so\np_left = 0.5 + e * (p_impression - 0.5). Most people have e near 1 (follow\ntheir impression), e near 0 is pure guessing, and a few people with e < 0 have\nreversed the task and pick the sequence that looks less random.\n\nIncumbent description: refinement of complement_symmetry_aversion.''')\nold='''    # Personal lapse (guessing) rate.\n    mu_lapse = pm.Normal(\"mu_lapse\", mu=-2.0, sigma=1.0)\n    sigma_lapse = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_lapse\", sigma=1.0)\n    z_lapse = pm.Normal(\"z_lapse\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=MAX_PARTICIPANTS)\n    lapse = pm.Deterministic(\"lapse\", pm.math.sigmoid(mu_lapse + sigma_lapse * z_lapse))\n'''\nnew='''    # Personal signed engagement: q = sigmoid(.) in (0, 1), engagement = 1 - 2q.\n    # q < 0.5 follows the impression, q = 0.5 guesses, q > 0.5 reverses the task.\n    mu_q = pm.Normal(\"mu_q\", mu=-2.0, sigma=1.0)\n    sigma_q = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_q\", sigma=1.0)\n    z_q = pm.Normal(\"z_q\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=MAX_PARTICIPANTS)\n    engagement = pm.Deterministic(\n        \"engagement\", 1.0 - 2.0 * pm.math.sigmoid(mu_q + sigma_q * z_q)\n    )\n'''\nassert old in src; src=src.replace(old,new)\nold='''    lam = lapse[participant_id]\n    p_left = pm.Deterministic(\n        \"p_left\", pt.clip(0.5 * lam + (1.0 - lam) * p_engaged, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n    )'''\nnew='''    e = engagement[participant_id]\n    p_left = pm.Deterministic(\n        \"p_left\", pt.clip(0.5 + e * (p_engaged - 0.5), 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n    )'''\nassert old in src; src=src.replace(old,new)\nopen('iter_3/candidate_4/candidate.py','w').write(src)\nEOF\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run1/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate \\\n    --candidate-dir /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_4 \\\n    --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5"}],"uuid":"9e001441-4515-4e2e-91bd-a5a4807b6ea3","session_id":"02